Objective: 
Find the password inside a file only accessible by bandit14 using a private SSH key.

Commands used:
ls - lists the contents of the current directory.
cd /etc/bandit_pass - Changes directory according to the given path.
ls -la - Lists the contents in a long listing format and shows hidden files too.
cat bandit14 - Checks the contents of the file.
cd - Changes directory.
exit - Closes the connection.
scp -P 2220 bandit13@bandit.labs.overthewire.org:/home/bandit13/sshkey.private . - Secure copies the file in bandit13 to my own current directory which is the "." at the end. When using scp -P is for port and for ssh -p.
chmod 700 sshkey.private - Changes mode so basically the permissions.
ssh -i sshkey.private bandit14@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220 - ssh using the private key given to us. -i means to identify 
cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit14 - Opens the file at the end of the given path.

