Notes:
Chmod changes the file permissions so something like this -rwxr-xr-- .
The first character tells us whether it's a file or a directory.
Next 3 are the owners permissions then the group permissions and others. So r - read,  w - write,  x - execute.
                                                                            100 so 4    010  so 2    001  so 1    like in binary 001 = 1, 010 = 2, 011 = 3
Using chmod you can give full permissions to everyone like this : chmod 777 <file>

